# --- Corrections (a reading the syllabic-consonant rule no longer reaches) ---

# squirrel (#209): the rule used to append a schwa-less reading after any vowel
# but `IY`, which reached `squirrel` (right — it rhymes with `curl`) and
# `liberal`, `femoral`, `referral`, `deferral`, `epidural` and `postdoctoral`
# (wrong — none of them does). `ER` is now an unabsorbing vowel, so the rule
# reaches none of the seven. Six of those are the fix; `squirrel` is the one
# real reading it cost, and it is asserted here instead. Both readings are
# genuine: two syllables (`SKWIR-ul`, with `referral`) and one (`skwirl`, with
# `curl`). ER L, with `curl`.
squirrel S K W ER1 AH0 L
squirrel(1) S K W ER1 L

# --- Corrections (one syllable before `l`, and three wrong sources, #232) ---
#
# The syllabic-consonant rule gives `dial` the one-syllable reading AY L, so it
# rhymes with `mile`, but only on a reading that ends in the `l`: `dialed` keeps
# its schwa and misses `wild`. Each plain -s or -ed form below has a base word
# that scores on the one-syllable key, and is given that reading beside its own.
# Ruled in #232, written in #253.

# gruel (#253): read with one syllable, UW L, so it rhymes with `cool` (#232).
gruel G R UW1 AH0 L
gruel(1) G R UW1 L
# accruals (#253): `accrual` scores on UW L; the plural joins UW L Z (#232).
accruals AH0 K R UW1 AH0 L Z
accruals(1) AH0 K R UW1 L Z
# denials (#253): `denial` scores on AY L; the plural joins AY L Z (#232).
denials D IH0 N AY1 AH0 L Z
denials(1) D IH0 N AY1 L Z
# dialed (#253): `dial` scores on AY L; the -ed form joins AY L D, with `wild` (#232).
dialed D AY1 AH0 L D
dialed(1) D AY1 L D
# dowels (#253): `dowel` scores on AW L; the plural joins AW L Z, with `owls` (#232).
dowels D AW1 AH0 L Z
dowels(1) D AW1 L Z
# duals (#253): `dual` scores on UW L; the plural joins UW L Z (#232).
duals D UW1 AH0 L Z
duals(1) D UW1 L Z
# dueled (#253): `duel` scores on UW L; the -ed form joins UW L D, with `cooled` (#232).
