# skier (#253): upstream also reads `S K AY1 R`, which put it with `fire`; it is "SKEE-er" only (#232).
skier S K IY1 ER0
# noir (#253): upstream `N OY1 R` rhymes it with `employer`; it is "nwahr", with `car` (#232).
noir N W AA1 R
# boudoir (#253): upstream `D OY2 R` is the same mistake as `noir`; it is "BOO-dwahr", with `car` (#232).
boudoir B UW1 D W AA2 R

# --- Corrections (a beat on the last syllable that CMUdict does not mark, #233) ---
#
# A word earns Points on its last stressed syllable, main or secondary (ADR-0020,
# amended 2026-10-25). Each word below is said with a beat on its last syllable
# that CMUdict leaves unmarked, so it is given secondary stress (`2`) there and
# nothing else changes. The compounds were found by the sounds-level test (both
# halves are words, the tail rhymes on its key) and then read by hand. Ruled in
# #233, written in #253.

# heretic (#253): "HAIR-uh-tick", a beat on -tic, so IH K with `trick` (#233).
heretic HH EH1 R AH0 T IH2 K
# limerick (#253): "LIM-er-rick", a beat on -rick, so IH K with `trick` (#233).
limerick L IH1 M ER0 IH2 K
# pyramid (#253): "PEER-uh-mid", a beat on -mid, so IH D with `grid` (#233).
pyramid P IH1 R AH0 M IH2 D
# aqualung (#253): compound, aqua + lung; joins AH NG with `lung` (#233).
aqualung AE1 K W AH0 L AH2 NG
# babysit (#253): compound, baby + sit; joins IH T with `sit` (#233).
